E. Zero-Copy IPC

- Shared-memory communication.
- Binary message formats.
- Producer-consumer coordination.
- Ring-buffer management.
- Buffer wraparound testing.
- Synchronization and message-integrity checks.

Important: Shared memory alone does not guarantee zero-copy operation. The implementation must avoid unnecessary payload copies and verify the behavior through testing.

