10. Benchmarking Strategy

Run repeatable workloads with different order volumes, such as:

- 10,000 orders.
- 100,000 orders.
- 1,000,000 orders, subject to available resources.

Measure:

- Total orders processed.
- Total trades executed.
- Orders per second.
- Trades per second.
- p50 latency.
- p95 latency.
- p99 latency.
- Maximum latency.
- CPU and memory consumption.

Use the same workload and environment when comparing different implementations.

Report whether latency includes only the matching operation or the complete order-to-response path. Keep the two measurements separate.

Do not claim a performance target has been achieved until the benchmark has actually run.

